L0215: Control flow violates a logical or termination promise

This control-flow form is not permitted in the current total or logical computation. An unconstrained loop may diverge and cannot define a logical value. Use structurally checked recursion or a supported decreasing measure rather than relying on expected runtime behavior.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/loop_in_math_fn.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
// A `loop` in a function that promises to return.
#[terminates] #[no_panic] #[no_io] fn first(n: u8) -> u8 {
    loop {
        break n
    }
}
```

Language, as built: [1.25:2](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.25:2).
